<p>The Pan-American Exposition was held from May 1 to November 2, 1901. The fair featured the latest technologies, including electric lighting, and attracted nearly 8 million people. A midway provided rides and other entertainment, and various athletic events were held. Several states, as well as South and Central American countries, had their own buildings. Although the event was originally intended for Niagara Falls, it was held in Buffalo because of that city's significantly better rail connections. {% person "nikola-tesla" %}Nikola Tesla{% endperson %} had also recently installed a three-phase alternating-current power transmission system, allowing designers to light the exposition using power generated 25 miles away at Niagara Falls. The Electric Tower was illuminated nightly by thousands of colored bulbs and floodlights.</p>

