<p>The 1901 Pan-American Exposition is often remembered as the setting for the assassination of U.S. President {% person "william-mckinley" %}William McKinley{% endperson %}. The president addressed attendees on September 5 and returned to the exposition the following day. On September 6, {% person "leon-czolgosz" %}Leon Czolgosz{% endperson %} shot McKinley outside the Temple of Music. McKinley died eight days later, and {% person "theodore-roosevelt" %}Theodore Roosevelt{% endperson %} became president on September 14, 1901.</p>
